    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13256" root="دهدى" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْدُوَّةٌ</span></b>  [app. originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْدُوْيَةٌ</span>, like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوَّةٌ</span> is
held by some to be originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُوْيَةٌ</span>,] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْدِيَّةٌ</span>
[likewise originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْدُوْيَةٌ</span>], and the latter also
without teshdeed [for alleviation of the utterance]:
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دُهْدُوهٌ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ده</span>.

